/* About: Test Configuration Defaults

Placeholder. This add-in has no environment-dependent tests yet, so
there is nothing to configure - the file exists so the hook is already
wired when that changes.

JMPOSIPITools uses its copy of this file for PI server / timezone
settings that vary per machine. The pattern: put defaults here, and
override them on a given machine by copying this file to
testConfig.local.jsl (gitignored). Both are loaded by
<RunTestsStandalone.jsl>, local second so it wins.

Add a setting here only when a test genuinely can't run without knowing
something machine-specific. Anything a test can determine for itself
belongs in the test.

Section: Globals
*/

